---
// sow-230 / sow-243 / sow-323: THE PAID-PLAN INVITE LANDING. Formerly /linkedin-invite/, renamed by owner
// ruling 2026-08-15: "coupon drives the offer, lander drives the copy." Since 2026-09-11 the chrome lives
// once in src/components/invite/InviteLander.astro; this page is campaign data, copy, and two story sections
// passed through the component's slots.
//
// WHY THIS DIRECTORY IS STILL CALLED curator-invite. The route does not move, because a private invitation
// link carrying it is already in circulation and a rename would 404 every copy that has been sent. The folder
// name is now history rather than a tier claim: it records where the link points, not what the page offers.
//
// RETARGETED TO THE SUPPORTER TIER ON 2026-09-12 (sow-323). The owner collapsed the two paid plans into one,
// so the tier this page used to advertise is no longer offered (house/membership-tiers.yml carries
// `offered: false` on it) and the plan that remains includes publishing. Left pointed at the old tier, the
// page would sell a plan nobody can buy. THE ONE LINE THAT MUST NEVER DRIFT is the tierDisplay('member')
// call below: every sentence here takes its label and its price from house/membership-tiers.yml through it.
// The coupon flow is untouched, so a link already sent keeps working and now lands on accurate copy.
//
// THE BENEFIT CARDS ARE RENDERED FROM THE REGISTRY, NOT WRITTEN HERE (sow-243). This page used to carry five
// hand-written cards beside a registry that listed the tier's real benefits; the member page had already
// proved that a hand-written list is where a tier claim escapes review. If a benefit belongs on this page, it
// belongs in the yml first.
//
// The two story sections below (a home for your work; where we meet) are this page's own copy. They describe
// the network rather than the plan, so they carry no benefit or price claim; they ride in the slots so no
// line of them sits in the shared template.
import InviteLander from '../../components/invite/InviteLander.astro';
import { BILLING_PERIOD } from '../../lib/membership';
import { tierDisplay } from '../../lib/tiers';

// sow-323: ONE paid plan. Named for the tier it resolves, because `const curatorTier = tierDisplay('member')`
// would work and would be a false name, which is how a lander advertised the wrong tier once already.
const memberTier = tierDisplay('member');
const TIER_LABEL = memberTier?.label ?? 'Network Supporter';
const TIER_PRICE_LABEL = `$${memberTier?.priceAnnual ?? 50}`;
const memberBenefits = memberTier?.benefits ?? [];

// THE FAQ ANSWERS THE OFFER, not the network in general; network context follows, and for a publishing tier
// that legitimately includes how content is stored. NO BENEFIT LIST HERE, NO REVENUE COPY (banned-patterns #2).
const faqs = [
  ['What does this invite give me?', `A full year at the ${TIER_LABEL} tier, with everything listed above, at no cost. It is a normal membership for the year, not a limited preview.`],
  ['Do I need a card to claim it?', 'No. No card is collected at any point during the free year, and nothing bills automatically.'],
  ['What happens when the free year ends?', `Nothing happens on its own. ${TIER_LABEL} is ${TIER_PRICE_LABEL} per ${BILLING_PERIOD} if you decide to continue, and you will not be charged unless you choose to.`],
  ['How do I claim it?', 'Sign in with GitHub from this page. Your coupon is already applied, so there is nothing to enter or remember.'],
  ['Can I pass this on to someone else?', 'It is meant for you, but the link works for whoever opens it first, so treat it as personal rather than forwardable.'],
  ['What is the GBTI Network?', 'A professional publishing network where members publish articles, projects, and prompts, for members only or for everyone. It combines a private community, weekly shop talk, and distribution support.'],
  ['What kind of content does the editorial team accept?', 'As a brand, GBTI can support a wide range of ideas and creative work. Our initial content will explore entertainment, education, technology, health, blockchain, developer relations, artificial intelligence, music, gaming, homesteading, and other subjects that interest our members. Members interested in publishing through GBTI can find our participation handbook inside the members area.'],
  ['How is my content and data stored?', "The public git repository is the database. Every article, product, prompt, and profile lives as a plain file in a public repo, and members publish by opening a pull request, by hand or through their own AI agents. There is no traditional CMS and no separate content database. The static site is the published read-view, and each member's client is their authoring node. Membership status is derived from Stripe rather than a separate user database, and every lookup matches on your immutable GitHub id."],
  ['Is all content public or private?', 'Both, and members come first. New work goes out to members, and a superadmin reviews it before it appears on the public website. For work that stays members-only, a stub with a short description appears on the public website, while the full content is readable by members inside the login-gated browser extension.'],
  ['Are comments on public-facing content also public?', 'By default, they are not, and can only be read inside the extension by other members. There is, however, the option to make a comment fully public.'],
  ['What happens during weekly shop talk?', 'A recurring two-hour session, live on Google Meet and coordinated on Discord, where members talk project development, track progress, share knowledge, set goals, and hold each other accountable to progress.'],
  ['What does GBTI stand for?', 'God Bless The Internet; a phrase that expresses appreciation and goodwill toward the continued growth and enrichment of the internet.'],
  ['Why is my first year free?', `The GBTI Network was founded by members of the Codeable network seeking a place to discuss the nuances of project development. This is a private invitation, so your first year at the ${TIER_LABEL} tier is on us.`],
] as const;
---

<InviteLander
  title="Your first year on us"
  description={`A private invitation: a full year at the ${TIER_LABEL} tier, first year free with your coupon.`}
  tierLabel={TIER_LABEL}
  tierPriceLabel={TIER_PRICE_LABEL}
  benefits={memberBenefits}
  benefitsHeading="What membership gives you"
  benefitsLead="Built for professionals who want a place to publish useful work, improve alongside other members, and belong to a network that rewards contribution."
  benefitsLayout="grid2"
  nav={[{ href: '#network', label: 'The network' }, { href: '#shoptalk', label: 'Shop talk' }, { href: '#benefits', label: 'Membership' }, { href: '#faq', label: 'FAQ' }]}
  hero={{
    titleHtml: 'Welcome to GBTI Network',
    lead: `GBTI is a professional publishing network for developers. Publish under your own name and build with people who ship. Your invite covers a full year at the ${TIER_LABEL} tier: full network participation, including content creation, no card required.`,
    ctaLabel: 'Claim your free year',
    secondaryCta: { href: '#network', label: 'How the network works' },
    // This page's own tier claims, true of the one paid plan it binds to (campaign data, not template).
    ticks: ['Publish under your own name', 'Weekly shop talk'],
  }}
  claimStyle="classic"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <Fragment slot="before-benefits">
    <!-- ================= WHY A NETWORK ================= -->
    <section id="network" class="ci-sec">
      <h2 style="max-width:20ch">A home for your work, without a site to run</h2>
      <p class="sec-lead">Most independent creators want to publish and be found, without standing up a CMS
        or paying to host and maintain a site. The network handles that, surfaces work to AI assistants, and
        adds the one thing most publishing collectives leave out.</p>
      <div class="grid3">
        <div class="card lift bcard">
          <div class="bod">
            <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="var(--ci-green-ink)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 4h16v14H4z"/><path d="M4 9h16"/></svg></div>
            <h3>No site to host or maintain</h3>
            <p>Publish without a CMS, hosting bills, or upkeep. Your work lives on the network and renders on
              your member profile.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card lift bcard">
          <div class="bod">
            <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="var(--ci-green-ink)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3v4M12 17v4M3 12h4M17 12h4"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3.5"/></svg></div>
            <h3>Built for AI recommendations</h3>
            <p>Content is structured so AI assistants can read and recommend it, which lifts how often your
              work gets surfaced.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card lift bcard">
          <div class="bod">
            <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="var(--ci-green-ink)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2v20M17 6H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6"/></svg></div>
            <h3>Built around the people who ship</h3>
            <p>A working network of professionals, not an audience. Members read each other, comment, and
              improve each other's work.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ================= SHOP TALK ================= -->
    <div id="shoptalk" class="ci-band">
      <div class="ci-band-in">
        <div>
          <h2 style="max-width:18ch">Where we meet, and hold ourselves accountable to progress</h2>
          <p class="sec-lead" style="max-width:52ch">Members gather for a recurring two-hour session to talk
            through project development, track progress, share knowledge, set goals, and keep each other
            accountable. It is the rhythm that turns publishing into momentum.</p>
          <div class="ci-pills">
            <span>Project development</span><span>Track progress</span><span>Share knowledge</span><span>Set goals</span><span>Accountability</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card ci-session bcard">
          <div class="bod">
          <div class="ci-live"><span class="dot"></span><span class="lbl">The session</span></div>
          <div class="ci-srow">
            <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="var(--ci-green-ink)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 2"/></svg></div>
            <div><b>Two hours, every week</b><span>A standing time members build their week around</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="ci-srow">
            <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="var(--ci-green-ink)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M15 10l5-3v10l-5-3z"/><rect x="3" y="6" width="12" height="12" rx="2"/></svg></div>
            <div><b>Live on Google Meet</b><span>Face to face with the people building it</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="ci-srow">
            <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="var(--ci-green-ink)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 15a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7l-4 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z"/></svg></div>
            <div><b>Coordinated on Discord</b><span>Where the conversation continues between sessions</span></div>
          </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</InviteLander>
